	(text "VFD INTERFACE - galvanically isolated (see vfd-interface-plan.md)\n- Isolation barrier runs through U15/U16/U17: board slot under each opto,\n   no copper in the keep-out, >= 6-8 mm creepage.\n- COM_ISO is MAINS POTENTIAL. Never tie COM_ISO/V15_ISO/+5V_ISO to GND, PE or enclosure.\n- GP20 VFD_PWM: ~1 kHz PWM. LED sinks into the pin -> 100 % duty = 0 V on VL1\n   (invert in FW). Set pad drive strength to 8 mA on GP20/GP21.\n- GP21 VFD_RUN: ~1 kHz square wave only while FW is healthy (re-arm every loop).\n   No edges -> Q3 releases X4 after ~20 ms. NOTE: GP20/GP21 share PWM slice 2 (A/B).\n- GP22 VFD_STAT: SP1 open-collector readback (P58 = 1 running / 3 fault). Low = active.\n- VFD: P10=2, P11=2, P53=5 (X4 fwd), P50..P52=0. E-stop stays hardwired.\n- D5 BAV99 (basic) replaces the plan's 2x BAT54 (extended); gate pumps to ~3.5 V.\n- Measure the VFD 15/24 V terminal before power-up (78L05 max 30 V, LM358 max 32 V).\n- J8 pin 4 (X5 / reverse) unused - reverse run channel not fitted.\n- F1, J8: no JLCPCB basic part available - LCSC number pending approval."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b1d173f7-35b4-4610-bcad-b657c8872aa5")
	)
